  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "One ticket to a show costs \\(\\$20\\) at full price. Susan buys \\(4\\) tickets using a coupon that gives her a \\(25\\%\\) discount. Pam buys \\(5\\) tickets using a coupon that gives her a \\(30\\%\\) discount. How many more dollars does Pam pay than Susan?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(5\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(15\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "A \\(25\\%\\) discount means Susan pays \\(75\\%\\) of the full price, while a \\(30\\%\\) discount means Pam pays \\(70\\%\\).\n\nSusan's four tickets cost \\(4\\cdot20=80\\) dollars before the discount, so she pays\n\\[\n80\\cdot0.75=60\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nPam's five tickets cost \\(5\\cdot20=100\\) dollars before the discount, so she pays\n\\[\n100\\cdot0.70=70\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nPam pays \\(70-60=\\boxed{10}\\) more dollars, choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
